WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:15.996
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is May twenty-eighth. Today's story is about aviation: a Japanese airline just launched its first flight with a brand-new airplane. Let's listen.

00:00:16.596 --> 00:00:27.995
<v News>今日、スカイマークは新しい飛行機「ボーイング737-8」の初めての便を飛ばしました。

00:00:28.696 --> 00:00:43.264
<v News>朝7時35分に羽田空港を出発して、福岡空港に向かいました。日本の航空会社がこの飛行機を使うのは初めてです。

00:00:43.963 --> 00:00:54.043
<v News>この飛行機は、今まで使っていた飛行機より燃料を約15パーセント少なく使うことができます。

00:00:54.743 --> 00:01:02.207
<v News>二酸化炭素の排出量も減るので、環境にやさしいと言われています。

00:01:02.908 --> 00:01:12.676
<v News>機内には充電ポートやコンセントがあり、乗客はスマートフォンやパソコンを充電できます。

00:01:13.376 --> 00:01:23.743
<v News>騒音が今までの飛行機より50パーセント少なく、パイロットも「静かすぎる」と驚いています。

00:01:24.444 --> 00:01:33.780
<v News>スカイマークは合計20機を注文しており、これから他の路線にも広げていく予定です。

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.111
<v Host>Let's break it down.

00:01:36.712 --> 00:01:38.272
<v Host>The opening line.

00:01:38.871 --> 00:01:44.751
<v Slow>新しい飛行機の初めての便を飛ばしました。

00:01:45.552 --> 00:01:48.599
<v Host>They flew the first flight of the new airplane.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.120
<v Vocab>便

00:01:51.519 --> 00:02:01.695
<v Host>Flight, or scheduled service. You'll see this word at airports and train stations. First flight, last flight. It counts transportation services.

00:02:02.296 --> 00:02:04.168
<v Host>A first for Japan.

00:02:04.768 --> 00:02:11.800
<v Slow>日本の航空会社がこの飛行機を使うのは初めてです。

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:17.039
<v Host>This is the first time a Japanese airline has used this airplane.

00:02:17.639 --> 00:02:20.544
<v Vocab>航空会社

00:02:20.943 --> 00:02:29.391
<v Host>Airline. The first two characters mean aviation. The last two mean company. Put them together and you get airline.

00:02:29.991 --> 00:02:32.271
<v Host>Why this airplane is special.

00:02:32.872 --> 00:02:42.592
<v Slow>今まで使っていた飛行機より燃料を約15パーセント少なく使うことができます。

00:02:43.391 --> 00:02:47.807
<v Host>It can use about fifteen percent less fuel than the airplane they used before.

00:02:48.407 --> 00:02:50.783
<v Vocab>燃料

00:02:51.183 --> 00:03:01.000
<v Host>Fuel. The first character means to burn. The second means material. Burning material. Cars, planes, they all need this.

00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:03.183
<v Host>Good for the planet.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:08.319
<v Slow>環境にやさしいと言われています。

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:14.711
<v Host>It is said to be environmentally friendly. You'll hear this phrase a lot in Japanese news.

00:03:15.312 --> 00:03:17.687
<v Vocab>環境

00:03:18.087 --> 00:03:25.936
<v Host>Environment. One of the most common words in news about climate and sustainability. Very useful to know.

00:03:26.536 --> 00:03:28.647
<v Host>What's new for passengers.

00:03:29.247 --> 00:03:35.872
<v Slow>乗客はスマートフォンやパソコンを充電できます。

00:03:36.671 --> 00:03:40.367
<v Host>Passengers can charge their smartphones and computers.

00:03:40.967 --> 00:03:43.415
<v Vocab>乗客

00:03:43.816 --> 00:03:54.472
<v Host>Passenger. The first character means to ride. The second means guest. A riding guest. You'll see it on buses, trains, and planes.

00:03:55.072 --> 00:03:57.280
<v Vocab>充電

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:08.048
<v Host>Charging. The first character means to fill. The second means electricity. Fill with electricity. You probably do this every day with your phone.

00:04:08.647 --> 00:04:10.903
<v Host>And it's surprisingly quiet.

00:04:11.503 --> 00:04:19.184
<v Slow>騒音が今までの飛行機より50パーセント少なくなりました。

00:04:19.983 --> 00:04:28.216
<v Host>Noise has been reduced by fifty percent compared to previous airplanes. Even the pilots say it's too quiet in the cockpit.

00:04:28.815 --> 00:04:31.120
<v Vocab>騒音

00:04:31.519 --> 00:04:40.567
<v Host>Noise. The first character means noisy. The second means sound. Unwanted sound. The opposite of music.

00:04:41.168 --> 00:04:44.168
<v Host>Let's listen to the full story one more time.

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:56.168
<v News>今日、スカイマークは新しい飛行機「ボーイング737-8」の初めての便を飛ばしました。

00:04:56.867 --> 00:05:11.435
<v News>朝7時35分に羽田空港を出発して、福岡空港に向かいました。日本の航空会社がこの飛行機を使うのは初めてです。

00:05:12.136 --> 00:05:22.216
<v News>この飛行機は、今まで使っていた飛行機より燃料を約15パーセント少なく使うことができます。

00:05:22.915 --> 00:05:30.379
<v News>二酸化炭素の排出量も減るので、環境にやさしいと言われています。

00:05:31.079 --> 00:05:40.848
<v News>機内には充電ポートやコンセントがあり、乗客はスマートフォンやパソコンを充電できます。

00:05:41.548 --> 00:05:51.915
<v News>騒音が今までの飛行機より50パーセント少なく、パイロットも「静かすぎる」と驚いています。

00:05:52.615 --> 00:06:01.951
<v News>スカイマークは合計20機を注文しており、これから他の路線にも広げていく予定です。

00:06:02.651 --> 00:06:05.387
<v Host>Quiz time. Three questions.

00:06:05.987 --> 00:06:10.427
<v Slow>この飛行機の名前は何ですか？

00:06:11.228 --> 00:06:16.052
<v Host>What is the name of this airplane? Boeing seven thirty-seven dash eight.

00:06:16.651 --> 00:06:21.740
<v Slow>燃料はどのくらい少なくなりましたか？

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:27.459
<v Host>How much less fuel does it use? About fifteen percent less than before.

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:31.755
<v Slow>機内で何ができますか？

00:06:32.555 --> 00:06:37.355
<v Host>What can you do inside the cabin? You can charge your smartphone or computer.

00:06:37.956 --> 00:06:50.339
<v Host>That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

00:06:50.939 --> 00:06:53.196
<v News>また明日。
